<title>USA: BPA leaves Thursday surplus power offers unchanged.</title>
<headline>BPA leaves Thursday surplus power offers unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) continued to offer only off-peak power for pre-scheduled sales on Thursday, the agency said Wednesday.</p>
<p>BPA continued to offer non-firm power for hours ending at 0600 and 2300 PDT at $9.50 per megawatt hour (MWh) for both Northwest and COB deliveries, while delivered prices for hours ending 0100-0500 and 2400 were flat at $9.00.</p>
<p>Firm power during off-peak hours on Thursday was also unchanged at $9.00 per MWh for all deliveries.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 212 955 6761))</p>
